{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_BOg6admP9A936f7pEMzJwNio","content":"1\t# Windows P1 INITIAL implementation bindings\n2\t\n3\tCreated 2026-10-11 UTC; the 20261010 filename is the agreed naming convention.\n4\tSupporting Planner, `harness-rules.md` section 1.5. Base: `93a61ba69504d6e9c1eee803c5ee4e2750c54640`.\n5\tThis is a **proposal**, not implementation, publication, functional acceptance or a state transition. `release_ready=false`.\n6\tRevision 1, 2026-10-11 UTC: proposes only the B001 native tuple/source closure requested after the fresh pre-scope BLOCKED verdict at `11c32d5806372ef3f7a7e9285d40f3b9c9e24a9b`. That verdict and the original c584 documents remain in git; this revision does not amend the critic's conclusion or authorize execution.\n7\t\n8\t## 1. Authority and exact paths\n9\t\n10\tThis addendum and adjacent `BL-WINDOWS-P1-INITIAL-BINDINGS-20261010.json` lock the INITIAL subset of the unchanged `BL-WINDOWS-P1-STAGES-20261009.md`. The earlier independent scope verdict found a coherent proposal, **not** approved implementation. Neither old proposal nor verdict is rewritten. The JSON holds exact constants, schemas and selection rows; the prose holds cross-field invariants that schemas alone cannot enforce. Both are required; disagreement blocks implementation.\n11\t\n12\tOnly these three **new** implementation files may be proposed by a later Generator:\n13\t\n14\t1. `docs/test-reports/windows-p1-stages-20261010/p1-stages.mjs` -- parent, probe, embedded guard/parser, offline validators and artifact sealing. No separate guard/helper file.\n15\t2. `tests/diagnostics/windows-p1-stages.test.ts` -- isolated synthetic/mocked checks only.\n16\t3. `.github/workflows/windows-p1-stages-diagnostic.yml` -- new dedicated diagnostic workflow.\n17\t\n18\tNo existing file may change, including original workflow/CLI/trace, `src/**`, worker, old tests/fixtures, dependencies/configuration, originals, state, harness or memory. The original 59-file/9-hash inventories remain the evidence references in the earlier scope verdict; this delivery does not re-authenticate that native run. All future source changes must be additions at the three exact paths above. Runtime outputs below are not source edits and must never be staged as implementation changes.\n19\t\n20\tBefore Generator dispatch: fresh independent pre-scope review of these two documents and explicit Coordinator scope approval. Before publication: independent actual-diff scope review, synthetic check execution and applicable **different-model-family** functional Evaluator acceptance, then separately authorized Coordinator publication. No worker pushes, no machine writes `pending_gate.decision`. This delivery executes none of those steps.\n21\t\n22\t## 2. INITIAL constants, environment and budgets\n23\t\n24\tThe JSON binds exactly four UTF-8/ASCII script strings and SHA-256 values. T1 is byte-exact original P1; T2 adds only the JSON writer pair; T3 adds only one bracketed `Get-Command` call. `Get-Command` may autoload: its markers bracket a lookup-or-autoload envelope, never a proven pure lookup. T0 tests only the writer/recorder. No T4/T5 constants, selectors, conditionally executable branches or module operations belong in the INITIAL artifact.\n25\t\n26\tNative call remains `powershell.exe`, exact prefix `-NoLogo -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command`, the fixed script operand, `shell:false`, `windowsHide:true`, and unchanged `runBoundedSubprocess`/worker. A fresh owned case/root, Node probe and bounded worker for each admitted variant; one PowerShell admission per case, **maximum four**, all smoke. No reuse, retries, warm parent, intentional native negative children, P2, arms or downstream cases.\n27\t\n28\tE0 / old-trace-on / common-guard-on only. Inherit case-insensitively only `PATH,SystemRoot,WINDIR,ComSpec,PATHEXT`; retain exactly the existing synthetic key set in JSON. `TW_PARITY_CASE=smoke`, `TW_PARITY_KIND=smoke`, `TW_PARITY_ARM=E0`, `TW_PARITY_TRACE=on`. Variant is determined by the fixed owned root basename and exact worker script/argv; **no new selector environment variable**. Empty Git config and owned HOME/TEMP behavior remain. No `APPDATA`, `LOCALAPPDATA`, `SystemDrive`, `PSModulePath`, environment fallback or command repair.\n29\t\n30\tUnchanged ceilings: workflow 12 minutes; diagnostic 600000 ms; case 40000 ms; cleanup/output allowance 3000 ms; operation 10000 ms; native 7000 ms; smoke/total launch caps 38/76; native combined output and counter 16384 bytes; case combined output 65536 bytes; each existing guard/trace stream 524288 bytes. Case admission and post-setup re-admission require remaining >=43000 ms and `used+1` within both caps. Native admission requires validated 7000 ms and remaining >=10000 ms; counter is recorded before spawn. Unknown clock/counter/identity aborts. No marker resets any deadline or allowance. Preserve worker's existing 1000 ms cleanup, 1000 ms startup/response watchdog and Windows additional cleanup handling; the 3000 ms diagnostic allowance does not change them.\n31\t\n32\t## 3. Timeout-safe owned observation and strict inclusive caps\n33\t\n34\tEmbed the copied guard semantics in the new CLI; load its `?guard=1` URL **before** the unchanged old trace import. The guard obtains the exact admitted PowerShell `ChildProcess` from the original async spawn and attaches additive Buffer listeners **before returning that handle** to trace/worker. Match case basename, worker path/payload, exact command/argv/script, budget and positive PID. Do not accept milestones from Node/Git/taskkill, a historical PID, another handle or only matching text. Do not `read`, `pipe`, `setEncoding`, replace/remove listeners, destroy streams, alter worker protocol/timers/results or write anything to worker stdout.\n35\t\n36\tParse LF/CRLF-terminated exact ASCII tokens only, split anywhere across Buffer chunks. No trim, substring, BOM, whitespace variants, blank lines, unknown text, duplicate/reordered/wrong-variant tokens or unterminated fragment. Bound the pending line to the longest admitted token plus CRLF (29 bytes INITIAL). Count stdout and stderr together; any stderr is invalid. Count rejected bytes as well. Maintain a saturating combined count at 16385 (the overflow sentinel), independently capped per-stream counts at 16384, and retain no raw fallback. Stop accepting markers after invalidity/overflow. Preserve the unchanged worker's own cap and termination behavior.\n37\t\n38\tEach complete accepted line is synchronously rebuilt and persisted as `native-fixed-stage` **inside the worker-process listener**, before timeout result construction can discard native stdout. Root polling while blocked in `runBoundedSubprocess` cannot substitute for this. `ordinal` is zero-based; arrival elapsed is observer monotonic time since owned native spawn, not cmdlet execution time. End events track each stream's actual `end`; `close`/destroy alone is not EOF. Emit exactly one `native-fixed-stream-end` at child close (or safe finalization), including both EOF flags. Missing end event itself is unknown. Strict event keys and safe types are in JSON.\n39\t\n40\tThe new stream state is invalid on parser violation/nonzero stderr/cap overflow; otherwise unknown on stream error or missing EOF; otherwise complete-sequence or complete-prefix. `eofObserved` equals both EOF flags. An incomplete clean sequence is a prefix, not success. First parser violation supplies its fixed reason, except overflow takes precedence. No raw text/error message/path/module object is persisted.\n41\t\n42\t**Strict append mechanism, not a pre-append race:** use one atomic `mkdirSync` lock per bounded file, with saved pre-trace filesystem primitives. Exact lock paths are JSON-bound. Under that lock, verify owned regular-file identity/no symlink, read current size, serialize the candidate to bytes, and append only if `size+candidateBytes <= cap`; exact cap is allowed. Counter parsing, limit checks and admission append are one transaction under its run-root lock. Contention, missing/corrupt identity, partial write, acquisition/release failure or overflow immediately fails evidence/health closed: no spin, wait, retry or stale-lock takeover. All permitted writers must pass this gate. Install the exact-path `fs.appendFileSync` wrapper before old trace captures it, then sync builtin exports, so old trace appends also use the gate without editing its source. No other filesystem target is wrapped; no raw log is uploaded. Lock operations using saved primitives are an explicit observation-I/O delta, not hidden parity. Existing strict read/rebuild/overflow suppression remains mandatory after writing. Do not claim that the old pre-append check itself provides a hard cap.\n43\t\n44\tPreserve live-owned-handle tree termination, watchdogs, observed-PID sampling, separate guard/trace health and retained-root rules from the frozen CLI. Never signal historical evidence PIDs or scan by process name. Neither a child close nor sampled dead PID proves entire-tree absence. EOF, guard/trace health, ownership/provenance and cleanup must each be trustworthy; none overrides another. Unknown retains roots under the original policy and blocks progression.\n45\t\n46\t## 4. Locked selection and root protocols\n47\t\n48\tApply the JSON table once, sequentially. `trustworthy` means strict root/probe/event identity and sequence, both EOFs, no stderr/overflow/abort, all expected guard/trace health complete, valid counter and known cleanup/provenance, including the closed native tuple/source relations below. A clean bounded refusal means an actual API return with worker `ok`, nonzero safe status, null signal and null error fields plus a permitted prefix, or an actual API timeout throw with worker `timeout`, the timeout error class, null error code and null unavailable return status/signal plus a permitted prefix. Launch/output/supervision/unknown are never clean refusal.\n49\t\n50\t### B001: native return/throw closure (required before selection)\n51\t\n52\t`native.metadataSource` is `api-return`, `api-throw`, `not-started` or `unknown`. It identifies an actually observed `runBoundedSubprocess` return/catch, not a conclusion inferred from trace or marker text. Native `status/signal` are **API return fields only**, never values copied from a Node worker's spawn-sync result or filled from native close facts on a throw path.\n53\t\n54\t| Path/outcome | Required native tuple and source |\n55\t|---|---|\n56\t| Normal return / completed | `metadataSource=api-return,workerKind=ok,status=0,signal=null,errorName=null,errorCode=null`; exact full marker sequence. |\n57\t| Normal return / clean refused | `metadataSource=api-return,workerKind=ok`, safe **nonzero** returned status, `signal=null,errorName=null,errorCode=null`; permitted clean prefix. |\n58\t| API throw / timeout | `metadataSource=api-throw,workerKind=timeout,status=null,signal=null,errorName=BoundedSubprocessTimeoutError,errorCode=null`. No invented status 0, EIO or inferred signal. |\n59\t| API throw / output, launch or supervision | `metadataSource=api-throw,status=null,signal=null`; respective actual API class. Output/supervision code is null; launch code is only the safe mapping of the actual `BoundedSubprocessLaunchError.code` (absent means null). Never clean refusal/progression. |\n60\t| Not started / unknown source | No unavailable return/error fields: status/signal/errorName/errorCode null. Not-started also has workerKind/elapsedMs null. Missing or unsupported actual error source is unknown, not a diagnostic error renamed as a product API error. |\n61\t\n62\tFor normal returns, require one uniquely admitted native childPid under the same owning worker PID, fixed case/root/script and spawn admission. Reconcile the returned native status/signal against **both** original guard and old-trace `child-exit` and `child-close` facts for that handle; all four facts must be present, unique and mutually equal to the returned tuple. `spawn-sync` status/signal refers to the Node worker and cannot satisfy this equality check. Native close/exit facts on a throw path are independent observations only; reconcile their ownership and mutual consistency, but do not copy them into unavailable return fields or guess what the API would have returned.\n63\t\n64\tMissing/duplicate/contradictory admission, API-source/error/worker relation or native exit/close tuple makes the observation unknown and blocks T1/T2 progression. Reject the conflicting raw protocol; rebuild only a safe unknown case, retaining independently observed facts/unknown flags rather than laundering a tuple into clean refusal. No worker partial-output change, extra native/host query or added surface is required or permitted. The existing EOF/health/cleanup/provenance requirements remain independent and unchanged.\n65\t\n66\t* T0 runs first; only exact writer success admits T1.\n67\t* **T1 success stops immediately**; T2/T3 are skipped. This is a conservative INITIAL narrowing approved by Coordinator, not a claim about an executed run. Clean T1 timeout/refusal with empty prefix admits T2; anything else stops unknown.\n68\t* T2 success stops. Only clean T2 timeout/refusal with exactly `[json-enter]` admits T3. No first marker, json-done without terminal, invalidity or any unknown stops; do not broaden.\n69\t* T3 is terminal whatever its result. Completed lookup with incomplete JSON does not authorize any other probe.\n70\t\n71\tEvery actual skipped case is `rootProcessStarted=false,nativeLaunches=0`. Unknown/missing post-crash records must not be fabricated as skips or zero admissions: nullable count/start fields and `decision=unknown` preserve uncertainty. Cases always appear once in T0-T3 order. `native_completed`, `prefix_protocol_valid`, `diagnostic_observation_complete` and release flags stay separate. A clean timeout prefix can be a complete observation of refusal, never a product PASS. Terminal markers alone cannot imply completion.\n72\t\n73\tThe probe writes one exact safe JSON root object, never its native bytes. Parent rebuilds the exact `probe`, `caseRecord` and `summary` schemas in JSON, re-derives script hash and stages from the owned guard log, and reconciles native admissions, original trace worker kind and expected PIDs. Safe product error classes/codes/signals use the frozen allowlists; new parser/selection reasons stay diagnostic-local. Reject extra/missing keys and unsafe values. Root protocol stderr must be empty. Preserve original case output cap and canary checks, with no raw fallback.\n74\t\n75\t## 5. New workflow, outputs and upload boundary\n76\t\n77\tThe new workflow is push-only for `codex/windows-p1-stages-ci-20261010`, with a matching job-level ref/event check, `contents:read`, `cancel-in-progress:false`, `windows-latest`, Node22 and 12-minute ceiling. No dispatch/PR/schedule/other branch, Secrets, environment, deploy, production, permission escalation or checkout credentials. Checkout `${{ github.sha }}`, depth 1, `persist-credentials:false`; independently verify actual HEAD equals it. Lock dependencies with `npm ci`; do not modify lockfiles. Workflow shell commands may orchestrate the job, but no extra native diagnostic PowerShell children or version probes are authorized.\n78\t\n79\tCommands/modes are locked in JSON. Prepare provenance, install dependencies, run only the new synthetic test file, run INITIAL once only after checks pass, seal safe evidence with `if:always()`, verify the sealed file set, then upload **only** that explicit set. Native execution remains future authority, not a command run by this Planner. No extra custom CLI scripts/selectors/timeouts. Importing the new module for tests must not install the guard or execute the diagnostic.\n80\t\n81\tScratch: `docs/test-reports/windows-p1-stages-20261010/.scratch/`; sealed upload: `docs/test-reports/windows-p1-stages-20261010/upload/`. Fresh create/no reuse. Owned temporary roots remain distinct from old outputs. Rebuild public JSONL only from validated guard/trace events; invalid/missing streams become empty safe public files with case unknown/invalid flags, never raw copied files. A typed incomplete diagnostic artifact may be sealed; malformed/unsafe provenance or core schema cannot. Missing run outcomes remain unknown, not synthetic success/zero counts.\n82\t\n83\tBefore upload require exactly the JSON-listed 16 files, no extras/symlinks, bound sizes, exact schemas/cross-field checks, no raw canaries, validated execution/source identity, and manifest SHA-256/size equality. The manifest hashes the other 15 files, not itself. Upload uses explicit paths (no directory/glob/scratch/temp/log fallback), artifact `windows-p1-initial-${{ github.sha }}`, seven-day retention, `if-no-files-found:error`. Upload occurs only after seal and immediate verifier success, even if the diagnostic is incomplete. Provenance distinguishes candidate execution SHA, this planning base, all current source hashes and original historical run; a later docs commit must not masquerade as executed identity. No PowerShell version or module provenance assertion is introduced.\n84\t\n85\t## 6. Required future checks and remaining boundary\n86\t\n87\tSynthetic/mock checks: every token split/LF/CRLF/coalescing; timeout prefix persistence; missing EOF/end event/error/health; unknown/BOM/non-ASCII/blank/unterminated/canary/stderr; order/variant/handle/PID/script mismatch; exact cap and +1 for native/case/guard/trace/counter; concurrent append contention and aggregate append size; 38/76 counters/time admission; independent cleanup/trace/provenance unknown; all selection rows and zero skipped launches; strict extra-key rejection; no import side effects; exact source/workflow/upload path set. These are obligations, **not performed tests**.\n88\tThe B001 control must reject `refused/status=1/workerKind=ok` carrying launch error/EIO, timeout carrying invented status 0/EIO/signal, canonical returned refusal whose admitted native close says status 0, missing/duplicate/wrong-owned-child exit or close, and error fields without actual API source. Exercise these at both T1 and T2 boundaries: observation unknown, no next native launch. Canonical normal return and canonical timeout still require all unchanged independent safety conditions; this revision does not claim those controls have run.\n89\t\n90\tThere is no unresolved *path/script/schema/selection binding* deferred to implementation in this proposal. Actual additive-listener/lock correctness, perturbation, runner provenance, clean EOF availability, PowerShell internals, whole-tree absence and all release gates remain unverified. Any feasibility failure or requirement for another file/delta blocks Generator and returns to Planner; it is not discretion to widen scope. No age/key/off-host-backup work is included. This delivery supplies only the two new documents, author-side static consistency checks and a local exact-path commit; no implementation, native test, CI, network, install, push or release claim.\n91\t\n92\tAuthor-side static result (2026-10-11 UTC): JSON parses; all four script hashes, ten referenced input hashes, frozen safe code/signal/abort enums, local schema references and exact required-key sets agree; three implementation paths and sixteen upload paths are distinct and consistent. These checks assess document consistency only, not functional correctness or independent scope acceptance.\n93\tRevision-1 author-side schema-only check: canonical normal return/timeout tuples satisfy the written native definition; eight contradictory source/error/status/signal tuples do not. This is document counterexample evaluation, not execution of the future B001 functional controls or independent review of this revision."}
